---
/**
 * Problem — the drift narrative, the four failure modes, and the Insight
 * pull-quote that answers them.
 *
 * Copy is rendered verbatim from docs/copy.md §Problem and §Insight
 * (ADR-0003: the copy deck is the single source of truth). The Insight
 * pull-quote lives inside this section rather than in a seventh component,
 * preserving phase-0's six-component structure (OVERVIEW.md §2.3).
 *
 * Every copy string sits on ONE source line — a wrapped version renders the
 * same text, but this way the built output greps literally against the copy
 * deck (the convention established in phase-1-ws-1.1).
 *
 * No copy string is split by an inline element and no em dash is generated
 * from CSS, for the same reason: `<strong>Scope creep</strong> — …` in
 * dist/index.html would fail a literal grep for the list item. The failure
 * list is "styled" through the list marker, dividers and spacing only.
 *
 * Reveal (ADR-0005): the section opts into the page's shared observer with
 * `data-reveal`, and its four blocks carry `.reveal` so they fade up in
 * reading order. The stagger delays live in the style block below; the
 * mechanism lives in index.astro. Nothing here sets a hidden base state — the
 * rules below render the finished section, and the reveal is opt-in motion
 * layered on top (the never-invisible rule).
 */
---

<section id="problem" class="section" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="reveal">A single long agent session drifts.</h2>

  <p class="lead reveal">It loses scope. It re-explores code it already understood. It fixes things nobody asked it to fix — and then it marks its own homework.</p>

  <ul class="failures reveal">
    <li>Scope creep — files touched that no one asked for</li>
    <li>Self-review — the author grading the author</li>
    <li>Lost context — every session re-discovers the last one</li>
    <li>Mechanical fumbles — walking YAML, comparing slugs, evaluating booleans</li>
  </ul>

  <figure class="insight reveal">
    <blockquote>
      <p>Everything an agent fumbles should be deterministic tooling, not agent judgment.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <!-- The leading em dash is part of the attribution copy, so it is a real
         character in the markup, not a CSS ::before that no grep can see. -->
    <figcaption>— the one rule metis is built on</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .lead {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* --- Failure modes ----------------------------------------------------- */
  .failures {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
    /* Drops the UA list indent. --space-0 rather than a literal 0: tokens.css
       defines the zero step, so spacing reads from the scale even when it is
       nothing (f-003). */
    padding: var(--space-0);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    list-style: none;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .failures li {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-4);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  /* Owl-gold marker square, used sparingly per OVERVIEW §3.2. Purely
     decorative: it carries no text, so it has no contrast obligation and
     nothing is lost when the pseudo-element is unsupported or unstyled. */
  .failures li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: var(--space-0);
    /* Optically centres the 4px square on the first line of a
       --leading-normal (1.6) body line: (1.6em - 4px) / 2. */
    inset-block-start: calc((1.6em - var(--space-1)) / 2);
    width: var(--space-1);
    height: var(--space-1);
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* --- Insight pull-quote -----------------------------------------------
     figure/figcaption rather than a nested <footer>: the caption is the
     quote's attribution, and ADR-0004 makes <footer> placement a landmark
     question this section has no business raising. */
  .insight {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-7);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-4);
    /* Decorative accent rule — the quote's boundary is its indentation and
       type size, so this bar carries no information of its own. */
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
  }

  .insight blockquote p {
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-lg), 3vw, var(--text-2xl));
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .insight figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* --- Reveal stagger ----------------------------------------------------
     Choreography only: this component decides the order its blocks arrive
     in, index.astro owns the animation itself. The delays are plain custom
     properties, so they are inert until the page's rule reads them — which
     it only does once `is-revealed` lands and only outside reduced motion.
     No media query is needed here for the same reason.

     80ms apart, four blocks, last one starting at 240ms: the section is
     fully settled 540ms after it arms, well inside a single scroll gesture.
     The h2 takes the 0ms default and so needs no declaration. */
  .lead {
    --reveal-delay: 80ms;
  }

  .failures {
    --reveal-delay: 160ms;
  }

  .insight {
    --reveal-delay: 240ms;
  }
</style>
